Drop @inlinable, @usableFromInline and @_fixed_layout

OpenCombine is not written for library evolution. This framework is built with
-enable-library-evolution, because apps link it the way they link Apple's
Combine, and the compile fails on these attributes there: keeping them gives
48 errors, starting with "'let' property 'box' may not be initialized
directly" in AnyPublisher.swift.

None of the three is part of a mangled name, so this changes none of them.
What it costs is cross-module inlining of `Subscribers.Demand` arithmetic and
the `AnyPublisher`/`AnySubscriber` boxes.

